ock"}, {"resource": "repository:python/owl/rs.pyi"}, {"resource": "repository:docs/rl-api-specs.md"}, {"resource": "repository:src/rules_engine/generation.rs"}, {"resource": "repository:docs/rules-engine.md"}, {"resource": "repository:docs/rules-parity-coverage.md"}]
41:Adding the vendored crate unifies `serde_json/arbitrary_precision`, exposing a test-only float decode incompatibility in starter `src/rules_engine/generation.rs`. The fixture enum now reads `serde_json::Number` and checks conversion to finite f64; production game logic and oracle comparisons are unchanged. Missing official Orbit fixtures were regenerated with `kaggle-environments==1.32.7` and replays downloaded using `kaggle==2.1.0`; `docs/rules-engine.md` and `docs/rules-parity-coverage.md` record the retained coverage. This preserves starter regression discipline rather than claiming Kaggriculture parity. The retained final `rs-prepare` log reports 155 passed, zero failed, two ignored, with formatting, all-target Clippy and documentation freshness checks; intermediate missing-fixture, decode and stale-doc failures are retained in the final receipt.
45:The contracts above have been inspected in the source during implementation. The native implementer reports Cargo check/build passing. The vendored engine unit suite passes120/120 (`cargo +stable test --manifest-path engine_rs/Cargo.toml --lib --locked`), with its final log independently read and hashed in the setup receipt. Four external test fixtures were made self-contained after preserved missing-file failures. The proper maturin abi3 wheel on CPython3.12.13/Torch2.9 passes **20/20 native environment/codec/reward tests**, including complete719-step termination/autoreset, seat-private isolation, caller-buffer reuse, serial/Rayon parity, rollback, grammar replay, economic counters/reset and disjoint rank seed streams. Current manifest verification pins exact source hashes, commands, toolchain and retained failures. Python typing for seven game files and root Clippy pass; Linux execution was outside that initial receipt; the later fused-path GPU evidence above closes that platform-execution gap. The pinned nightly installation initially lacked its rustc-driver library; Rustup repaired the partial installation to `1.97.0-nightly (e9e32aca5 2026-04-17)`. The original pinned-toolchain `rs-prepare` then passed all 155 cases with two existing ignored, formatting, Clippy and documentation freshness; stable 1.94.1 verification is also retained. The repair and final pinned-toolchain logs were independently read and retained, so the initial local toolchain gap is closed. An unsupported direct dylib import test harness exited 139 before the proper maturin wheel environment was prepared; no such copied module is retained. The final shared receipt adds 772 passing Python cases and actual single/two-process CPU PPO updates. Source-scoped status does not extend these checks to future-engine parity or playing strength. The CPU adapter timing and later complete GPU measurements have separate explicit workload limits.
# Task 0.3 — failed training status and traceback ordering

Base: `559a3956b769200ed183ee7d42fa40f59b79b7f9`, branch `kg/rebuild-codex`.
Scope: rebuild plan Task 0.3 and reference-branch gap-closure Task 1.1.
Target: successful logger sessions finish with code 0; exceptions and interrupts
finish with code 1 and propagate; rank-tagged tracebacks reach stderr before
distributed teardown. Stop after unit checks, cookbook documentation and commit.

## TDD steps

1. Add offline W&B finish forwarding and DebugLogger interface tests. Add logger
   session success/failure tests and strengthen existing runner integration tests
   to assert exact close codes. Test RuntimeError, KeyboardInterrupt and SystemExit.
2. Add distributed failure tests capturing stderr inside the mocked cleanup call;
   assert the original exception propagates and cleanup runs exactly once.
   The clean base has no CPU/Gloo diagnostic hook: mock CUDA/NCCL using the
   existing test pattern instead of importing reference-branch behavior.
3. Run the focused tests and preserve their expected failing result before any
   production edit. Implement the reference plan's three production changes.
4. Repeat the focused tests, then run:
   - `uv run pytest tests/owl tests/scripts tests/tools -m "not slow" -q`
   - `uvx --from rust-just just py-prepare`
   - `cargo test` (rebuild plan's retained Rust unit regression requirement)
   Review mapped README documentation. All commands stay offline and local;
   no training, evaluation, CUDA execution or remote W&B session.
5. Record actual outcomes and limitations under `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/`, add
   cookbook note/index/log, review the final diff, and commit on this branch.

The old plan's `--extra reference` does not exist on the clean base; use the
owner's explicit verification commands. The plan's named superpowers skills
are not installed in this Codex session; native read-only subagent review covers
the test plan and implementation. Claude cross-review remains required before
merge; no merge or other worktree operation is part of this task.

## Pre-implementation review

A native Codex reviewer confirmed the minimal production patch applies. Its
recommendations are included above: exercise runner wiring, interrupts, exact
close/cleanup counts and exception identity. Boundaries: traceback printing is
before process-group destruction, after logger finalization; hard kills, startup
before the distributed try block, and failures inside cleanup are not repaired.
